FO,
Here is a reference regarding mean centering and collinearity.  There is nothing wrong with mean centering for other purposes, such as giving the parameters a desired interpretation, but it does not help with collinearity.  I agree with Terry that there is rarely anything to be gained from centering dummy variables.

Mean-Centering Does Not Alleviate Collinearity Problems in Moderated Multiple Regression
Models  Author(s): Raj Echambadi and James D. HessSource: Marketing Science, Vol. 26, No. 3 (May - Jun., 2007), pp. 438-445

Keith

